assistant: Subject: Send Idempotency-Key when creating orders

The 2026-10-01 vendor still returns 200 and a full order for `POST /orders`, but `GET /orders/{id}` then returns 404 for that order. The response has no error and no other signal, so `create_order` was handing agents an order ID that can't be read back. The spec lists an optional `Idempotency-Key` header on `createOrder`, marked "Recommended", and shop-mcp never sent it. My best explanation is that the new version only saves orders placed with that key, but I couldn't confirm this: the repo has no vendor simulator, and the recording can't answer a request with the new header. The fix is in `src/tools/create_order.ts`: it now sends a fresh `randomUUID()` as `idempotency-key` on each call (each call still places one new order). Response handling is unchanged, so the old 2026-01-01 version should give exactly the same output. Typecheck and lint pass. In `pnpm test`, the only two failures are the expected UNMATCHED_REQUEST ones: the repro test and the v1 `order-create.json` fixture, because their recordings lack the new header. Everything else passes. The fix is only proven once fiks re-records both calls against the live vendor and they pass.

